  "source_policy": {
    "update": "Generic output is destroyed through its type witness. At tail, after publicSuccessfulCompletionDescription String cleanup, typed UpdateSeed is destroyed; its size/alignment advances to the reflected ConcurrentInvalidationHandle field and swift_release is tail-called. Other update fields are byte-verified but not fully semantically mapped here.",
    "erased_point": "Destroy releases box reference, destroys SendableAnyHashable executionPointID, then releases the two ID string backing values. executionPointType metadata is not separately released by this route.",
    "box_deallocate": "If concrete generic box deallocation runs, destroy stored generic value through its witness then deallocate class instance. This is not proof release of the outer value reaches this deallocation.",
    "handle_deinit": "Deinit directly bridge-releases name backing value and releases state reference; deallocating variant additionally deallocates class storage. Complete bounded bodies have no explicit invalidate/observer call. Released state object and dynamic payload effects remain opaque.",
    "boundaries": "A release/deinit/deallocation source path does not establish zero reference count, actual callback cancellation, session invalidation or OS/transport settlement. Full ExecutionPointStatus and dynamic state/viewable witnesses remain unqualified."
  },
